  "question": {
    "text": "Find the electric flux (in S.I. unit) through the rectangular plate&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>abcd</mi></math> of length <math><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>, width&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> and whose centre is at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> from an infinite line of charge with linear charge density <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>36</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. Consider that the plane of the frame is perpendicular to line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>P</mi></math>.<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0076_0dbd163ce65f.png\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 173px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "0.5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0076_762aedac64cc.jpg\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 253px;\" /></p><p>If we arrange three more rectangular plates (similar to the one which is given)&nbsp;around the wire, then we get a rectangular box open at both ends. We bring two more plates and use them to close this rectangular box. We can see from the figure that we have a symmetric system for which the total flux is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence the flux through one plate is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p>"
  }
}